      "title": "How this one keeps your angle",
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfyui-pixaroma",
        "Node name for S&R": "PixaromaNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\": 1, \"content\": \"<h1>KEEPING YOUR ANGLE</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Whatever you set up in the 3D view is what you get: the angle you turned to, how close you zoomed, and where you dragged the object with the right mouse button. The picture is painted on top of your view instead of being composed from scratch, so an object pushed off to one side stays off to that side.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Denoise</h2><p>One setting does this, on the sampler. It is set to <span style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\">0.70</span> and it decides how much freedom the model gets:</p><table class=\\\"pix-note-grid\\\" style=\\\"--pix-note-grid-border: #f66744; --pix-note-grid-header-bg: #1a1a1a\\\"><thead><tr><th>Denoise</th><th>What you get</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>0.50</td><td>your view is kept, but the rough edges of the 3D mesh come back</td></tr><tr><td><b>0.70</b></td><td><b>your view is kept and the surfaces come out clean</b></td></tr><tr><td>0.85</td><td>it starts re-composing, so the object drifts and changes size</td></tr><tr><td>1.00</td><td>your framing is ignored. That is workflow 5</td></tr></tbody></table><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Those were measured on the same 3D view with the same seed, so they compare. If the result looks too close to the raw 3D model, raise it a little. If the object starts moving around, lower it.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"question-mark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Picture size</h2><p>There is no size list here, on purpose. The picture comes out at the size of the photograph taken of your 3D view, and that is the <span style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\">width and height on the Load 3D node</span>. Change those two numbers, then drag once inside the 3D view so it takes a fresh photograph at the new size.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Which one to use</h2><ul><li><b>This one</b> when the angle is the point: you posed the model and you want that exact shot, cleaned up.</li><li><b>Workflow 5</b> when you just want a good picture of the object and do not mind where it ends up. It composes the shot itself and it has the size list.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\", \"buttonColor\": \"#f66744\", \"lineColor\": \"#f66744\", \"width\": 480.0, \"height\": 925.0, \"backgroundColor\": \"#2a2a2a\"}"
      ],
      "color": "#14436c",
      "bgcolor": "#2a2a2a"
    }
